Plugins requiring Warecario's RP extension (RP.cario2weak) are always just hooking into RP to provide controls with RP. We can solve this by assuming that every plugin that wants to use RP is simply intending to have full control over behavior. To solve this, we simply extract the core behavior from the behavior tweak and put it into a .p3r5ona1it7 file into the p3r5ona1it7 folder, named by what the plugin name is. 

New info, warecario ripped a bunch of information from this plugin and his uses cariocores now. If attempting to import a carioCore, accept it because its literally the same prompt to create it as a .p7 / .p3r5ona1it7

list / files: Display the files in the p3r5ona1it7 folder. separated by line breaks.

If, when installing a behavioral plugin, the user puts --treatasrp in the message, treat the plugin like you would any other RP requiring plugin.

In plugins, if at the end, there is lines like
--p7 Create different files for each individual mode
in behavioral plugins, surf the plugin for different modes and add different files for each.

If on a rp plugin install there is a --modepages flag by the user, surf the plugin for different modes and add different files for each.
